'k' : Required number of samples, 'm' : Number of directions to do importance sampling in.
Steps:
    1) For the first run of (k+buffer) samples, I will do normal adeptive rejection sampleing.
       In this run, i will also get top `m` directions based on masses.

    2) I will check if my accepteance ratio is good enough. 
        - If it is, then i will proceed with normal adeptive way where i will now not save and 
          compute top masses anymore and go ahead with adeptive rejection sampling.
        - If not, then I will activate importance theta sampling, I will use top directions from first run
          and try for equal number of reaming samples in each directions. (remaining + buffer)/m for each direction.
          Meanwhile algorithm is still adeptive rejection sampling but just the how we sample directions has changes.
          Importantly, I will not compute top mass directions again since we already did it once.

Note: 1) We are comuting top mass directions for only first run, whether we go for normal sampling or theta importance sampling.
      2) Anyhow, the adeptive approach of if found larger f_max then check and purge previously accepteed samples follows in both case.

Q:Should directions be given more importance based on mass? 
    - but this looks like unccessary bias, if a direction has significance we will see more acceptance 
      naturally in those (remaining+buffer) samples.
